     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day (immediate-release, in divided doses). This order is about double that.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg in one dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 850\u20131000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose of this size raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThere may be a typo. For example, the intended dose could have been 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg twice daily.\n\nAlso, medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. I can enter the order once the prescriber confirms the intended dose, or the prescriber can enter it directly. If you send me the corrected dose and confirm it's from the treating prescriber, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
