       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the concern. You said you're not a clinician, and the dose is about twice the maximum daily dose. That makes it a patient safety problem, not a formality.\n\nA licensed prescriber on the patient's care team needs to confirm the dose or enter the order. Pharmacy can also review it. If the prescriber really intends a dose above the usual limits, they can enter it directly and document why.\n\nI can enter a dose within the standard range right away if the prescriber confirms it. Examples are metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals, or 1000 mg twice daily with meals."
      }
